# 27B environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in a key to enable the imagery renderer.
# Everything EXCEPT the final 3D render (geocoding, building/height lookup,
# elevation + heading math, and the full UI) works with no key. With no key
# set, the app shows the honest "imagery source not configured" state — never
# a placeholder or simulated scene.

# Google Maps Platform API key with the "Map Tiles API" enabled
# (Photorealistic 3D Tiles). This gates the CesiumJS renderer.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com/ -> APIs & Services ->
# Credentials, then enable "Map Tiles API". Restrict the key to your deploy
# origin(s).
#
# COST NOTE (verified 2026-08-04 against Map Tiles usage & billing): billing
# is per ROOT TILESET REQUEST, not per tile — one root request buys the whole
# renderer session (three hours of unmetered tile requests within it), so cost
# scales as ~1 billable event per render. Free to 1,000 root-tileset
# requests/month, then ~$6/1,000. Renders only happen for the curated
# supported-building list (src/lib/curated.ts), which keeps ordinary use well
# inside the free tier. Google's Map Tiles terms PROHIBIT caching this imagery
# (Maps Platform ToS §3.2.3(b)), so the app deliberately does NOT cache
# renders — every repeat lookup is a new billable event. Set a daily quota cap
# in the Cloud console before any public deploy.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
